## Summary

Define the StorageBackend interface/trait that enables pluggable storage backends. This abstraction allows switching between memory, link-cli, and custom backends via configuration.

## Background

Following [code-architecture-principles](https://github.com/link-foundation/code-architecture-principles):
- **Interfaces & Abstraction**: Hide implementation details behind stable contracts
- **Configuration Over Code**: Scale from embedded to distributed without code changes

## Requirements

### StorageBackend Interface/Trait
```typescript
// TypeScript
interface StorageBackend {
  // Core operations
  save(link: Link): Promise<LinkId>;
  load(id: LinkId): Promise<Link | null>;
  delete(id: LinkId): Promise<boolean>;
  query(pattern: LinkPattern): Promise<Link[]>;

  // Batch operations
  saveBatch(links: Link[]): Promise<LinkId[]>;
  deleteBatch(ids: LinkId[]): Promise<boolean[]>;

  // Metadata
  getCapabilities(): BackendCapabilities;
  getStats(): BackendStats;

  // Lifecycle
  connect(): Promise<void>;
  disconnect(): Promise<void>;
  isConnected(): boolean;
}

interface BackendCapabilities {
  supportsTransactions: boolean;
  supportsBatchOperations: boolean;
  durabilityLevel: 'none' | 'fsync' | 'replicated';
  maxLinkSize: number;
}

interface BackendStats {
  totalLinks: number;
  usedSpace: number;
  operations: {
    reads: number;
    writes: number;
    deletes: number;
  };
}
```

```rust
// Rust
#[async_trait]
pub trait StorageBackend: Send + Sync {
    async fn save(&self, link: Link) -> Result<LinkId>;
    async fn load(&self, id: LinkId) -> Result<Option<Link>>;
    async fn delete(&self, id: LinkId) -> Result<bool>;
    async fn query(&self, pattern: LinkPattern) -> Result<Vec<Link>>;

    async fn save_batch(&self, links: Vec<Link>) -> Result<Vec<LinkId>>;
    async fn delete_batch(&self, ids: Vec<LinkId>) -> Result<Vec<bool>>;

    fn capabilities(&self) -> BackendCapabilities;
    fn stats(&self) -> BackendStats;

    async fn connect(&mut self) -> Result<()>;
    async fn disconnect(&mut self) -> Result<()>;
    fn is_connected(&self) -> bool;
}
```

### Backend Registration
```typescript
// Register custom backend
LinksQueue.registerBackend('my-custom', MyCustomBackend);

// Use via configuration
const queue = new LinksQueue({
  backend: { type: 'my-custom', options: { /* ... */ } }
});
```

## Deliverables

1. [ ] TypeScript interface definitions in `src/backends/types.ts`
2. [ ] Rust trait definitions in `src/backends/traits.rs`
3. [ ] Backend registry/factory implementation
4. [ ] Documentation with custom backend example
5. [ ] Ensure API parity between JS and Rust

## Dependencies

- #7 - Link interfaces

## Enables Parallel Work

Once completed, the following issues can be worked on in parallel:
- link-cli backend (JS)
- link-cli backend (Rust)
- Other custom backends

